From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] firmware: arm_scmi: set up Tx/Rx channel for ACPI-activated
 protocols

Patch 0093 activates every firmware-implemented SCMI protocol under ACPI
(the ACPI namespace has no per-protocol child nodes to drive
scmi_create_protocol_devices from the DT path). But it creates each
protocol's device WITHOUT first setting up that protocol's Tx/Rx channel,
which the DT path does via scmi_txrx_setup() before scmi_create_protocol_devices().

Without the channel setup a protocol has no entry in info->tx_idr, so
do_xfer() -- which outside RAW mode has no Base-channel fallback -- returns
-EINVAL for every transfer on that protocol. This silently kills genpd:
SCMI_PROTOCOL_POWER (0x11) registers no power domains, so the consumers
that depend on them (panthor GPU CIXH1003, armchina NPU CIXH4000, linlondp
display) touch unpowered MMIO and hang the SoC (~5.96s AXI lock observed on
cixmini). VPU (amvx) does not use genpd and is unaffected.

Mirror the DT / 7.0.x sky1-next ACPI path: call scmi_txrx_setup(info, NULL,
prot_id) for each ACPI-activated protocol before creating its device. Under
ACPI there is no per-protocol channel fwnode, so pass NULL; mailbox_chan_available(NULL, idx)
returns false and scmi_chan_setup() takes the Base-channel alias fast path
(no fwnode dereference).

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [downstream ACPI enablement for CIX Sky1]
---
 drivers/firmware/arm_scmi/driver.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/arm_scmi/driver.c b/drivers/firmware/arm_scmi/driver.c
index b38d764..1b99613 100644
--- a/drivers/firmware/arm_scmi/driver.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/arm_scmi/driver.c
@@ -3383,6 +3383,17 @@ static int scmi_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 			if (idr_find(&info->active_protocols, prot_id))
 				continue;
 
+			/* Set up the protocol's Tx/Rx channel before creating its
+			 * device.  Under ACPI there's no per-protocol channel node;
+			 * pass NULL fwnode so scmi_chan_setup() aliases this protocol
+			 * to the Base channel.  do_xfer() has no Base fallback outside
+			 * RAW mode, so without this the protocol has no tx_idr entry
+			 * and every xfer returns -EINVAL, silently killing genpd
+			 * (SCMI_PROTOCOL_POWER 0x11) -> GPU/NPU hang.
+			 */
+			if (scmi_txrx_setup(info, NULL, prot_id))
+				continue;
+
 			ret = idr_alloc(&info->active_protocols, (void *)np,
 					prot_id, prot_id + 1, GFP_KERNEL);
 			if (ret != prot_id)
-- 
